From 8ee4419261a00b73e0ceeb58d3fbd024717f6a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Mehltretter <kmehltretter@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 01:08:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] module: reject invalid relocation section target indices
To: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@kernel.org>,
    Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>,
    Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>,
    Sami Tolvanen <samitolvanen@google.com>
Cc: Aaron Tomlin <atomlin@atomlin.com>,
    Nicolas Pitre <nico@fluxnic.net>,
    Russell King <rmk+kernel@arm.linux.org.uk>,
    Ard Biesheuvel <ardb@kernel.org>,
    linux-modules@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

The module loader validates section contents and names before calling
module_frob_arch_sections(), but does not validate the sh_info target index
of relocation sections. Several architecture hooks use that value as a
section-table index before apply_relocations() later skips invalid indices.

On ARM32 with ARM_MODULE_PLTS, an out-of-range SHT_REL sh_info makes
module_frob_arch_sections() form a pointer outside the section table and
read its sh_flags. A malformed module therefore causes a kernel paging
request instead of being rejected.

Reject relocation sections whose target index is outside the section
table during the early ELF validity pass.

Fixes: 7d485f647c1f ("ARM: 8220/1: allow modules outside of bl range")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: LLM Frama-C
---
Found with Frama-C Eva at b9b3e33b70b7 using a source-identical ARM32
module_frob_arch_sections() slice. An unconstrained loader-permitted sh_info
produced an invalid section-table pointer alarm. A reproducer is available.

A/B tested at b9b3e33b70b7 with GCC 15.2.0 on ARM32 QEMU virt/TCG using
multi_v7_defconfig plus VMSPLIT_2G. The control module loaded and unloaded.
Before this change, a module differing only in one SHT_REL sh_info (10 to
0x10000000) oopsed at module_frob_arch_sections()+0x160. After this change,
the same module was rejected with ENOEXEC and the control still loaded.

The full patched ARM32 zImage also builds without warnings at the stated base
commit with the same compiler and configuration.

 kernel/module/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/module/main.c b/kernel/module/main.c
index d0e1e0bd2ad0..30c7a05488bc 100644
--- a/kernel/module/main.c
+++ b/kernel/module/main.c
@@ -1933,6 +1933,7 @@ static int elf_validity_ehdr(const struct load_info *info)
  * * Section array fits in the user provided data
  * * Section index 0 is NULL
  * * Section contents are inbounds
+ * * Relocation section target indices are inbounds
  *
  * Then updates @info with a &load_info->sechdrs pointer if valid.
  *
@@ -1983,6 +1984,12 @@ static int elf_validity_cache_sechdrs(struct load_info *info)
 	/* Validate contents are inbounds */
 	for (i = 1; i < info->hdr->e_shnum; i++) {
 		shdr = &sechdrs[i];
+		if ((shdr->sh_type == SHT_REL || shdr->sh_type == SHT_RELA) &&
+		    shdr->sh_info >= info->hdr->e_shnum) {
+			pr_err("Invalid ELF relocation section target index %u\n",
+			       shdr->sh_info);
+			return -ENOEXEC;
+		}
 		switch (shdr->sh_type) {
 		case SHT_NULL:
 		case SHT_NOBITS:

